      "thm:panel-experiment-transfer"
    ],
    "justification": "This matching lower bound and attainment theorem is the field-level payoff: it quantifies the exact risk-certificate cost through moving donor constraints.",
    "gap": "CanenSong2026SimplexWeight proves uniform validity for a fixed optimizer. FreybergerRai2018UniformBands, Definition 1, restricts attention to bands induced by a nonrandom-shape set and rules out random selection among valid bands; Section 2.3 leads with weighted area, and its generic-objective Theorem 2 is accompanied by low-level sufficient conditions and a worked approximation specifically for weighted area. Independently of those results, the unresolved target is the unrestricted externally randomized local max-curve-diameter value and its sharp transfer to a synthetic-control panel.",
    "consumer": "Software implementing the displayed fixed-ridge quadratic simplex estimator can report how much simultaneous risk uncertainty is information-theoretically unavoidable near the chosen donor-face geometry.",
    "proof_tex": "Let \\(q=1-\\alpha\\). Theorem \\(\\mathrm{thm:certified\\mbox{-}gaussian\\mbox{-}value}\\) gives, for each \\(\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{opt}}>0\\), a bounded finite padded-envelope Gaussian rule with coverage \\(q\\) and worst-case expected loss at most \\(L_\\alpha+\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{opt}}/3\\). Apply the panel-to-Gaussian kernel, pad for the uniform target error, and mix with the full local envelope to repair vanishing undercoverage. Undoing centering and \\(\\sqrt n\\) scaling gives observed-panel intervals satisfying\n\\[\n\\liminf_n\\inf_{u\\in\\mathcal U}P_{\\theta_n(u)}\\{R_{P_{\\theta_n(u)}}(v_n(t))\\in\\widetilde C_n^{(\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{opt}})}(v_n(t))\\ \\forall t\\in\\mathcal D\\}\\geq q\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n\\limsup_n\\sup_{u\\in\\mathcal U}\\mathbb E_{\\theta_n(u)}\n\\left[\\sup_{t\\in\\mathcal D}\\sqrt n\\,\\operatorname{diam}\\widetilde C_n^{(\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{opt}})}(v_n(t))\\right]\n\\leq L_\\alpha+\\varepsilon_{\\mathrm{opt}}.\n\\]\nThus the sequence is in the panel honesty class.\n\nConversely, suppose a panel-honest sequence had, along a subsequence, worst-case scaled expected width at most \\(L_\\alpha-\\epsilon\\). Center, scale, and clip its sections to the deterministic local envelope. Coverage is preserved and loss becomes bounded. The reverse kernel followed by target padding gives Gaussian bands with coverage \\(q-o(1)\\) and risk at most \\(L_\\alpha-\\epsilon+o(1)\\). A mixture with the full Gaussian envelope of probability \\(o(1)/\\{\\alpha+o(1)\\}\\) restores coverage \\(q\\) at cost \\(o(1)\\), contradicting the definition of \\(L_\\alpha\\). This proves the lower bound.\n\nChoose \\(\\varepsilon_k\\downarrow0\\) and increasing \\(n_k\\) such that coverage deficit, transfer error, and excess risk are at most \\(\\varepsilon_k\\) for \\(n\\geq n_k\\). Use rule \\(k\\) for \\(n_k\\leq n<n_{k+1}\\), with the repair mixture. The diagonal sequence is honest; its limsup loss is at most \\(L_\\alpha\\), and the converse makes its liminf at least \\(L_\\alpha\\). Its primal rules and dual bounds are the certified finite ones. The global projection band \\(C_n\\) is not used.",
